within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.N_NervousSystem.N06D_AntiDementiaDrugs.N06DX04_Lecanemab;
model Lecanemab_Bhagunde2026v2_PD_gfap
  "linear exposure-response sweep — Bhagunde_2026_2 :: GFAP (plasma GFAP)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Interfaces.PartialExposureResponseSweep(
    E0 = 3.15e-07,      // [kg/m3; pg/mL × 1e-09]
    Emax = 0, EC50 = 1,      // unused by a line
    exposure_per_s = 1);
  parameter Real slope = 0.237   "[logit]";
equation
  response = E0 + slope*exposure;
  // family_inferred: the record's model family is disease_progression; read from the parameters: a slope and no Emax — linear
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 1000, Interval = 2),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Lecanemab_Bhagunde2026v2_PD_gfap</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Bhagunde P et al., <i>Alzheimer's &amp; dementia (New York, N. Y.) 12:e70246</i> 2026 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/trc2.70246\">doi:10.1002/trc2.70246</a>) — plasma GFAP [pg/mL] against lecanemab — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: linear.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =        315 pg/mL    drug-free response (baseline) (Baseline GFAP (pg/mL), Q324)
  slope =      0.237 logit    change in response per unit of exposure (SLP (logit), Q335)</pre><p>The algebra is <code>response = E0 + slope*exposure</code>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one  of lecanemab per second of simulated time: there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 3.15e-07   (drug-free)</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Bhagunde_2026_2: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Lecanemab_Bhagunde2026v2_PD_gfap;
